ance indicators in 2017 compared with 22% in 2021.\"}]}, {\"v\": \"surveillance/descriptive\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"AFR countries conduct case-based measles surveillance\"}]}], \"methods_quotes\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"using annual administrative coverage data (number of doses administered divided by the estimated target population)\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"A previously described model for estimating measles cases and deaths was updated with measles case data and United Nations population estimates data during 2000–2021\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"State-space model of unobserved measles incidence generated using inputs from all AFR countries except South Sudan\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"To calculate incidence, only countries that reported data are in the numerator and denominator.\"}], \"confidence\": \"high\", \"uncertain_fields\": []}", "type": "text"}]}